> Generate random values, weighted picks, and noise patterns.

name Random
slug bookshelf-random
version 5.0.0
tags runtime

$dim[1d]:
  since: 2026/11/23 26.4
  where: on a line
$dim[2d]:
  since: 2024/08/05 1.21
  where: on a plane, such as the ground
$dim[3d]:
  since: 2026/11/23 26.4
  where: in a volume


feature function choice > Select a random value from a list.
  authors SBtree
  since 2024/06/17 1.21
  input arguments
    options: [any] @ 1.. > values to choose from
  output storage: any > value chosen
  output result: int > index of the value chosen

feature function weighted_choice > Select a random value from a list, each with its own weight.
  authors Aksiome
  since 2024/09/04 1.21
  input arguments
    options: [any] @ 1.. > values to choose from
    weights: [int @ 0..40000] > weight of each value, in the same order, for at most 256 values: a value of weight 2 is picked twice as often as one of weight 1
  output storage: any > value chosen
  output result: int > index of the value chosen

feature function simplex_noise/$dim > Get the simplex noise value at a position $dim.where.
  authors Aksiome
  contributors SBtree
  since $dim.since
  input storage
    pos: [int] @ 1..3 > block coordinates, as many as the noise has dimensions
    size: int @ 1..2097152 > width of a noise cell, in blocks: a larger cell gives a smoother noise
    seed: int > seed of the noise: the same seed gives the same noise
  output storage: float @ -1..1 > noise value at the coordinates

feature function fractal_noise/$dim > Get the fractal noise value at a position $dim.where: layers of simplex noise added from coarse to fine.
  authors Aksiome
  since $dim.since
  input storage
    pos: [int] @ 1..3 > block coordinates, as many as the noise has dimensions
    size: int @ 1..2097152 > width of a noise cell, in blocks: a larger cell gives a smoother noise
    seed: int > seed of the noise: the same seed gives the same noise
    octaves: int @ 1..16 > number of layers: more layers add finer details
    persistence: float @ 0..1 > amplitude of each layer relative to the previous one, such as 0.5
    lacunarity: float @ 1..8 > frequency of each layer relative to the previous one, such as 2.0
  output storage: float @ -1..1 > noise value at the coordinates

feature context_int_provider uniform > Get a random integer, every value in the range being equally likely.
  authors Aksiome
  since 2024/06/24 1.21
  input storage
    min: number > lowest value
    max: number > highest value
  output result: int > random integer from min to max, both included, their fractions dropped

feature context_float_provider uniform > Get a random number, every value in the range being equally likely.
  authors Aksiome
  since 2026/11/21 26.4
  input storage
    min: number > lowest value
    max: number > highest value
  output result: float > random number from min to max

feature context_int_provider binomial > Count the successes out of a number of trials, each with the same probability.
  authors Aksiome, SBtree
  contributors Aeldrion
  since 2024/06/15 1.21
  input storage
    trials: int @ 0.. > number of trials
    probability: float @ 0..1 > probability of success of each trial
  output result: int @ 0.. > number of successes, from 0 to trials

feature context_int_provider geometric > Count the trials until the first success, each with the same probability.
  authors Aksiome, SBtree
  contributors Aeldrion
  since 2024/06/16 1.21
  input storage
    probability: float @ 0<..1 > probability of success of each trial
  output result: int @ 1..65536 > number of trials, the success included

feature context_float_provider normal > Get a random number from a normal distribution, clustered around the mean.
  authors Aksiome
  contributors Leirof
  since 2025/05/15 1.21.5
  input storage
    mean: float > value the results are centered on
    spread: float @ 0.. > standard deviation: how far from the mean the results spread
  output result: float > random number, at most 6 spreads from the mean

feature context_int_provider poisson > Count the events that happen in an interval, given how many happen on average.
  authors Aksiome, SBtree
  contributors Aeldrion
  since 2024/06/16 1.21
  input storage
    lambda: float @ 0..10 > average number of events, by steps of 0.1
  output result: int @ 0.. > number of events
